From 2314a3be13caef5cb60bf1351d5e22e34c7a73f5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 07:16:53 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] www: themed confirm modal (USB format), guide link on About,
 flash-page cancel hardening

Three owner items for v2.7.3:

- reaper_util.js gains reaperConfirm(msg, {okLabel,cancelLabel,danger}, cb):
  a Reaper-themed in-page confirm replacing the browser-chrome confirm().
  Backdrop carries class 'ovl' so the shell re-anchors it to the visible
  slice (rule 35); message rendered via textContent; a danger dialog does
  not accept Enter - destruction takes a deliberate click; labels come from
  the CALLER's dict tokens. Reaper_USB.asp converts both native confirms
  (format = danger + Format/Cancel buttons, safely-remove = OK/Cancel).
  Other pages' confirm() calls are a later sweep.

- Reaper_About.asp links docs/REAPER-GUIDE.md from the links row (book
  icon, RABT_43/44 - people did not know the guide existed).

- Reaper_Firmware.asp: the backlog 'Cancel on the upgrade confirm leaves
  the buttons dead' report is NOT reproducible in current source - a
  node:vm harness running the page's real script proves every Cancel path
  (install confirm, both upload confirms, node-push confirm, veil dismiss)
  leaves busy=0 and all buttons live; the wedge class matches the
  pre-a0c115dc45 doubled-poll code. The one remaining wedge - an uncaught
  throw after busy=1 but before the veil paints - is now cleared by the
  global error handler (busy reset when no veil is up to dismiss).

Dicts: RABT_43/44 appended to all 25 packs, lockstep 6761. Host-validated:
all pages' JS parses, ASCII clean, modal harness confirms ok/cancel
callback semantics + overlay teardown.
